  "verifiedBehaviors": [
    "Launching CLI exits after explicit native commit while actual BFF health remains launch-bound; independent stop obtains native whole-generation completion. Two cycles include retaining the same committed generation from another CLI.",
    "Uncommitted EOF, original startup deadline, malformed/mismatched PID or commit, lost first receipt and lost commit ACK preserve their closed refusal or uncertainty semantics. No second start is admitted without matching committed ownership.",
    "Known no-child spawn failures and native no-supervisor-fork outcomes retire only their matching pending attempt. Root-zero not-started records never establish reap of an admitted generation.",
    "Application environment crosses the private control pipe as bounded KAE1 data. 140 benign entries/provider/certificate/browser values reach only the admitted app root, with selected identity/grant overrides. Native W/S environments stay closed.",
    "Native packet intake, supervisor generation creation and final root exec consume the same original monotonic grant. Independent physical delayed-supervisor controls observe late root execution before and none after under the same one-second grant.",
    "Native PID publication uses complete flushed staging and atomic rename; partial writes never expose a legacy prefix. Unknown/truncated capability markers remain refused.",
    "The existing SQLite exclusion primitive is shared. Canonical path aliases converge, state removal cannot replace the held sibling guard, and its nested .keiko location retains the existing workspace denial.",
    "Unexpected new observation failures propagate to their owning diagnostic path. Registered body-free native ownership and direct spawn-refusal outcomes are retained; no new catch exemption is added."
  ],
